        "heading": "Verify a certificate scope before you verify the mill",
        "body": "**A certificate scope** is the set of products, sites and processes that a certificate actually covers. A buyer checks the scope before the number, because a valid number on the wrong scope proves nothing about the goods. Certification for qualified buyer review covers four named scopes. They are GOTS, OEKO-TEX STANDARD 100 Class II, China Organic, and quality-system files. Each is available within that document's listed scope, and the [certificate check page](https://www.christopherbu.com/certificates/) records the public lookups.\n\nThe certificate numbers are provided with the written quotation and the shipping documents. That is the moment a buyer can check each one against the issuing body. A scope claim on a quotation is only a line of text until the public record agrees with it. Write the scope, the class and the lookup result into the checklist before the audit, so the visit is spent on the floor."
