        "heading": "What a buyer can state without guessing",
        "body": "A buyer can state three things safely. Each metric is a named per-batch field on the written quotation, and its result is recorded for a specific lot. The evidence is the per-lot grading certificate plus the test method reference. A numeric cut-off for any of the three is not one of them. Asking for the certificate on paper is the check; inventing a threshold is not. The [sample request page](/samples/) covers the swatch that should arrive with the quotation, but a swatch without a named test method proves only that the sample looked right.",
