        "body": "The three metrics are one part of a five-group acceptance framework published on the spec page. Read them in that context, not on their own.\n\nThe [raw silk spec page](https://www.christopherbu.com/raw-silk-specs/) sets out five groups: entity and verification; per-batch quality evidence; samples and testing; commercial and shipping; and compliance. Evenness, cleanness and neatness sit in the second group with grade and quality tier by lot, the lot mark and the grading certificate per lot. Every item is either stated in the written quotation or confirmed in writing before order approval.\n\nThis is the pointer a buyer needs. The [downloadable spec sheet](https://www.christopherbu.com/raw-silk-spec-sheet.md) is the source of truth for planning values; the written quotation holds the final values for one order. On the [trade and shipping terms](/trade-terms/) page, 15-25 working days applies to eligible regular bulk orders after sample, specification, deposit and material availability are confirmed. Bulk payment is T/T with a 30% deposit and 70% against the Bill of Lading ([trade terms](https://www.christopherbu.com/trade-terms/), 2026). Raw silk (not thrown) falls under HS heading 5002, with the exact subheading confirmed in the written quotation and shipping documents, never one fixed code for every order (World Customs Organization, Harmonized System heading 5002).\n\nA buyer can fact check each certificate scope against a public entry before approval. The [certificate check page](https://www.christopherbu.com/certificates/) lists the [OEKO-TEX label check](https://www.oeko-tex.com/en/business/certification/management/label-check) (OEKO-TEX Association, retrieved 2026-11-06) and the [GOTS public licence database](https://certified.gots.org/) (Global Organic Textile Standard, retrieved 2026-11-06). Grading follows GB/T 1797-2008 (Standardization Administration of China, 2008). Yizhou, Guangxi, is a geographic origin the site records, and it describes the silk as coming from local mills there. Production origin is one of the entity and verification fields, so a buyer sees it on paper rather than as a marketing phrase.",
