        "heading": "A pre-dispatch checklist",
        "body": "Work through these six lines before you release any raw silk shipment. The list is short enough to use at a desk and specific enough to catch a document mismatch.\n\n- Name the written quotation as the reference and keep the spec sheet and signed order documents beside it.\n- Read the HS subheading on the quotation, then confirm it matches the shipping documents. Heading 5002 alone is not a classification.\n- Check the spec sheet, lab dip, inspection report, packing list and certificate of origin as one set, not five forms.\n- Confirm the test method reference and ask which inspection report it governs.\n- Reconcile bale weights, lot marks, production origin and certificate numbers against the written quotation.\n- Fact check every certificate number against the public database, and confirm destination-market compliance in writing.\n\nBefore you approve dispatch, [request a written quotation](/contact/) and ask for the five-document set reconciled against it. A set that agrees with itself is a shipment a buyer can release."
