        "heading": "A familiar first order",
        "body": "Consider a first bulk enquiry. A buyer asks for 6A, 20/22D, and a unit price for comparison. The reply comes back with a grade, a denier and a price. The buyer approves. What never reached paper: the variety, the finish, the lot that the 6A claim covers, the grading certificate for that lot, the shade card reference, the HS subheading, or the certificate scope.\n\nWeeks later, a weaving run shows yarn that behaves differently from the approved sample. The buyer asks which lot the 6A claim described. The answer was never written down, because nobody asked for it at the start. The grade was there. The evidence behind it was not.",
