        "heading": "One root cause behind the confusion",
        "body": "One root cause explains the miss. The grade is the most compact line on a page, so it gets read as a summary of the whole order. A short label that looks complete is easy to treat as complete. The grade is one field inside a larger acceptance framework, and the fields around it are what make a shipment acceptable.\n\nThe [raw silk spec page](https://www.christopherbu.com/raw-silk-specs/) publishes that framework in full. It groups the grade with per-batch quality evidence, samples and testing, commercial and shipping terms, and compliance. A buyer who stops at the grade stops one line into the first group. Skimming is rational when comparing several suppliers in one afternoon. It is also the moment the rest of the specification disappears.\n\nThe [20/22D white raw silk yarn](/products/raw-silk/) page shows the product side of the same problem. It lists denier, grade and finish, which is the trio a first pass tends to stop at. The written quotation adds everything else. Read the whole page.",
