        "heading": "A quality tier assigned per lot",
        "body": "**A raw silk grade** is a quality tier that classifies one lot of mulberry raw silk yarn. The published spec sheet lists 4A, 5A and 6A as the tiers, and states that grade availability is confirmed by variety in the written quotation. Grading follows GB/T 1797-2008, and moisture is controlled below 11% (Standardization Administration of China, 2008). The [certificate check page](https://www.christopherbu.com/certificates/) names that standard as the grading reference.\n\nI will not set out numeric cut-offs between 4A, 5A and 6A here. The test methods and the classification belong to the standard and to the per-lot grading certificate. A sales line that invents a threshold for a tier would be a guess. What a buyer can state safely is narrower: the tier is a lot-level quality classification under a named standard, and the evidence behind it is a test result recorded for that lot.",
        "level": 3
