        "heading": "The lot, the certificate and the method",
        "body": "Three pieces of evidence make a grade checkable, and the grade itself is none of them. The lot mark names the batch. The grading certificate per lot records the result for that batch. The test method reference names the standard behind the result, GB/T 1797-2008. On the [downloadable raw silk spec sheet](/raw-silk-spec-sheet.md), the first two sit in the per-batch quality evidence group and the third sits in samples and testing.\n\nEvery field in the framework follows one of two paths. It is either stated in the written quotation, or confirmed in writing before order approval. The written quotation tells a buyer which applies. A buyer should ask for the per-lot grading certificate and the test method reference on paper before approving, because a grade with no lot and no method cannot be checked after the yarn arrives.",
