        "body": "The grade also says nothing about the transaction. Price and payment terms, incoterms, lead time, packing and bale specification, and HS classification are separate fields. On the [trade and shipping terms](/trade-terms/) page, 15-25 working days applies to eligible regular bulk orders after sample, specification, deposit and material availability are confirmed, with the binding schedule in signed order documents. Packing is export cartons or bales, 60 kg per bale typical, and luxury silk yarn comes in 5 kg bundles. Bulk payment is T/T with a 30% deposit and 70% against the Bill of Lading ([trade terms](https://www.christopherbu.com/trade-terms/), 2026).\n\nRaw silk (not thrown) falls under HS heading 5002, and the exact subheading is confirmed in the written quotation and shipping documents, never one fixed code for every order (World Customs Organization, Harmonized System heading 5002). Compliance is separate again. Certification for qualified buyer review covers GOTS, OEKO-TEX STANDARD 100 Class II, China Organic and quality-system files, within each document's listed scope. Certificate numbers come with the written quotation and the shipping documents. A 6A grade guarantees none of that.",
