        "heading": "One judgement method: anchor every grade claim three ways",
        "body": "Use one test on every grade claim. Ask for three anchors: the lot, the certificate, and the method.\n\nThe methodology is plain. Take a line that says 5A. The lot mark tells you which batch that claim describes. The per-lot grading certificate tells you the recorded result for that batch. The test method reference, GB/T 1797-2008, tells you which standard produced the result. A grade with all three is a checkable claim. A grade without them is a word on a page.\n\nFor instance, a buyer comparing two offers can put the three anchors in a short table: lot mark, certificate reference, method. Whichever offer names all three is the one that can be accepted against a specific shipment. The test takes a minute and it separates a specification from a sales line. It also gives the buyer three questions to send in writing, instead of one vague request for a better grade."
