        "body": "Put the grade in an enquiry as one line among several, and ask for the evidence on paper. Yizhou, Guangxi, is a geographic origin the site uses, and it describes the silk as coming from local mills there. Production origin is one of the entity and verification fields on the written quotation, so a buyer sees it on paper rather than as a marketing phrase.\n\n- State the denier you want, and note whether 20/22D or 27/29D applies.\n- Name the variety, and ask whether your grade is available for it.\n- State the finish: greige (undyed), a standard shade card reference, or a custom colour to order.\n- Ask for the grade and quality tier by lot, the evenness, cleanness and neatness fields, the lot mark and a grading certificate per lot.\n- Ask which test method reference the inspection report uses.\n- Ask for the certification scope and where the certificate number will appear.\n- Keep the spec sheet, the written quotation and the signed order documents together.\n\nThe specific action is simple. Before you approve an order, [request a written quotation](/contact/) and read the grade line next to the per-batch quality evidence group. The [sample request page](/samples/) covers the swatch that should arrive with the quotation. A grade that survives all of those checks is a claim a buyer can accept against a real lot."
