        "body": "The table below is the core of the decision. It lists the terms a raw silk buyer meets in a written quotation and a signed order, and sorts each one into lock or flexible. Read it as a working sheet. The left column names the term, the middle column holds the terms a buyer fixes in writing, and the right column holds the terms a buyer confirms in writing before order approval.\n\nTwo rows deserve a second look, because they are easy to read backwards. HS classification and certificate scope are locked as rules, not as values. A buyer fixes heading 5002 and the requirement that the exact subheading and the certificate numbers are confirmed in writing. The specific subheading and the specific numbers arrive later, with the quotation and shipping documents. Locking a made-up value early is worse than leaving it open. The [trade terms page](https://www.christopherbu.com/trade-terms/) states the subheading rule, and the [certificate check page](/certificates/) lists the verification entry points.",
