        "heading": "Should a buyer lock the unit price when volume rises?",
        "body": "A buyer can agree a price for one order, but the price is not the term that protects the buyer. The terms that define the goods should be fixed in writing regardless of the price. A lower unit price does not change grade, denier, packing or the quality evidence, so those stay locked. The price line moves; the conformance lines do not.",
