        "heading": "Where the figures on a written quotation come from",
        "body": "Every number on a written quotation traces to a published document. The spec sheet is the source of truth for planning values. The written quotation and the shipping documents hold the final values for one order. Confusing the two is a common cause of a mismatch at the document stage.\n\nDenier is 20/22D as standard, with 13/19D also in regular supply and 27/29D available on request. Grades span 4A, 5A and 6A, and grade availability is confirmed by variety in the quotation. Grading follows GB/T 1797-2008, with moisture controlled below 11% (Standardization Administration of China, 2008). The standard is named on the [certificate check page](https://www.christopherbu.com/certificates/).\n\nPacking is export cartons or bales, 60 kg per bale typical, and luxury silk yarn comes in 5 kg bundles. Bulk ships FOB Nansha, FOB Yantian, FOB Qinzhou or FCA Yizhou, with samples by DHL worldwide or a designated courier. Payment for bulk is T/T with a 30% deposit and 70% against the Bill of Lading ([trade terms](https://www.christopherbu.com/trade-terms/), 2026).\n\nRaw silk (not thrown) falls under HS heading 5002. The written quotation and shipping documents confirm the exact subheading, never one fixed code for every order (World Customs Organization, Harmonized System heading 5002). The same rule is repeated on the trade terms page. A buyer should check the subheading on the quotation, not assume a single code covers every shipment.\n\nFinish is greige (undyed) or dyed to order from a standard shade card or a custom colour. Both are available on all products. The [product range](/products/) lists four varieties: 20/22D white raw silk, natural dupion silk yarn, 1-ply luxury silk yarn, and GOTS-certified organic silk. **Greige** is silk yarn or fabric that has not been dyed.\n\nA useful check is to ask which figures are planning values and which are final. The spec sheet calls its own values planning values, checked against current availability before quotation. The written quotation carries the final spec, MOQ, schedule, applicable HS subheading and organic status. A buyer who compares a planning value with a final value will find a discrepancy that is not really there. The two documents answer different questions.",
